  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole, with a kickoff scheduled for July 15, 2023. The project involves leveraging AI for data visualization and real-time analytics, with a budget adjusted to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and a separate $15,000 approved for team training. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and prototype testing for secure file sharing ahead of schedule. The project is currently moving into the development phase, led by Omar Jensen, with user interface enhancements planned for October. The team is also exploring a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology and has requested stakeholder feedback on the prototype by the end of November."
